-- title:
--   Ordered adjacency after adding the directed bridge relation
-- statement:
--   For vertices in increasing order, adjacency in the supremum of `H` and the graph generated by the directed relation from `u` to `v` is exactly original adjacency or the ordered pair `(u,v)`.
-- source:
--   David P. Williamson and David B. Shmoys, The Design of Approximation Algorithms, Cambridge University Press, 2011, author electronic manuscript, Section 10.2, proof of Theorem 10.11, pp. 270-272. https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511921735. Bounded tree-width of the pieces: Robertson–Seymour (planar graphs of radius r have tree-width at most 3r+1) / Bodlaender (k-outerplanar graphs have tree-width at most 3k-1).

import Definitions.Def_WilliamsonShmoys_PlanarDrawingOn

open WilliamsonShmoys

theorem WilliamsonShmoys.bridge_augmented_graph_adj_iff__p2m_e1c10048_df1f_49a0_8080_5a203a611921_a4
    {V : Type} [LinearOrder V]
    (H : SimpleGraph V) (u v : V) (huv : u < v) :
    ∀ a b, a < b →
      ((H ⊔ SimpleGraph.fromRel (fun x y => x = u ∧ y = v)).Adj a b ↔
        H.Adj a b ∨ (a = u ∧ b = v)) := by sorry
